  "the container is the root Name of the site's .value chain; a write whose container is a call result (f()['a']['b'] = v) resolves to f and is published as such, so an expression-shaped container is visible in the chain column and never silently called a name",
  "binding precedence is parameter > loop target > local assignment > module scope > unresolved; a parameter reassigned inside the function is still published as a parameter, which is the conservative reading for a reachability claim",
  "'same name as a counted read receiver' is name equality inside one function, not an alias proof: two parameters with different names can hold one object, and the same name can be rebound between the write and the read. The face publishes the evidence for each row rather than a reachability verdict it cannot support",
